---
title: Institutional Goals and Objectives
summary: The goals and objectives that guide GCUA's formation of hearts, preparation of minds, and development of Spirit-empowered leaders.
---

# Institutional Goals and Objectives

## I. “GCUA exists to cultivate hearts…”

### Institutional Goals

GCUA will prepare students' hearts to steward and advance God's work.

GCUA will form Pentecostal students with spiritual discernment who reflect Jesus in their communities.

GCUA will cultivate hearts that desire and pursue Pentecostal empowerment within diverse ministry contexts.

### Institutional Objectives

GCUA will recruit students who hunger for Pentecostal life and biblical truth.

GCUA will form students' hearts for their communities through chapel, classroom discipleship, and supervised ministry practice.

GCUA will exhort and encourage students to pursue the gifts of the Spirit in classroom, chapel, and ministry settings.

## II. “GCUA exists to prepare minds.”

### Institutional Goals

GCUA will train students to root spiritual disciplines and theology in Scripture.

GCUA will establish a university-wide culture of assessment and continuous improvement.

GCUA will equip students intellectually to lead others in biblical practice and faithful doctrine.

### Institutional Objectives

GCUA will teach students to exegete Scripture responsibly and faithfully.

GCUA departments and offices will implement an institutional assessment plan to strengthen effectiveness.

GCUA will require students to apply biblical principles learned in class to ministry and academic settings.

## III. “GCUA exists to develop skills of Spirit-empowered leaders…”

### Institutional Goals

GCUA will educate students to become Christian leaders who discern and engage communities for God's glory.

GCUA will prepare students to serve in cultures resistant to the Gospel and become instruments of godly change.

GCUA will form Pentecostal ministers who refuse to compromise biblical truth.

### Institutional Objectives

GCUA will train students to practice the Great Commission in personal life and ministry leadership.

GCUA will provide mentoring that forms mature leaders anchored in biblical principles and practices.

GCUA will equip students to serve as leaders in both church ministry and academic settings with biblical integrity.
